<http://data.silknow.org/object/e20227c6-3bfc-358f-8523-1c2934dd406b/observation/1>
        a                   crmsci:S4_Observation ;
        ecrm:P2_has_type    <http://data.silknow.org/observation/technical-observation> ;
        ecrm:P3_has_note    "Picture made of tapestry-woven wool and silk on a linen warp. Depicting the Madonna and Child, after Guido Reni. The picture is oval with the spandrels being woven in stone-coloured wool. The Madonna leans over the outstretched body of the sleeping Child with hands joined in prayer. She is in half-profile to the left, wearing a white headcloth and robe with a blue cloak. The Child lies with his head on a red cushion at the left while one arm is bent back and the other is extended along his side.\n\nWoven in wool and silk on a linen warp, 16-18 warp threads to the inch, 6-7 to the centimetre."@en ;
        crmsci:O8_observed  <http://data.silknow.org/object/e20227c6-3bfc-358f-8523-1c2934dd406b> .

